11.      India has relaxed some trade restrictions and advanced its bilateral trade negotiations,
while some trade measures have been introduced or extended.
•
India further relaxed or removed export restrictions on agricultural products, including onions,
broken rice, and sugar, as domestic prices moderated. In addition, India has streamlined its tariff
structure and reduced the tariffs on a range of products, reducing the simple average industrial
tariff to 10.7 percent, from 13.5 percent in 2023. The import duty on cotton has been suspended
