Does the entity have any project related to reducing Green House Gas emission? If Yes, then provide details.

Yes.

The company has undertaken the following initiatives:

Increase in adoption of Solar Power at our large facilities - Top 15 facilities (by size) have a combined sanctioned load of
8 MW, of which 4.6 MW has been installed. Delhivery will continue to commission further installations.

Continued focus on fleet upgradation - In FY24, in a joint effort with our vendors, we added 191 tractors to our combined
fleet of tractors taking the total count to 753 at the end of FY24 from 562 at the end of FY23. We will continue this effort
through FY25 as well.

Continued focus on deploying CNG/EV/LNG powered vehicles - In FY24, over 1,600 vehicles as part of our permanent
fleet were powered by CNG/EV/LNG. We will continue this focus through FY25.

This combined will have a significant impact on reducing the intensity of our Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions.

We will also continue to reinforce Delhivery''s Sustainable Sourcing Policy which was introduced in FY23 through FY25.
